- butter
- flour
- milk
- half and half, or heavy cream
- at least three different kinds of cheeses. I usually try and go for a salty cheese, a melty cheese, and a sharp cheese
- pasta. hollow pastas thaat soak up sauce are preferred. 

cook your pasta al-dente and set aside. reserve some pasta water to add to your sauce later 
heat a saucepan over medium heat. melt your butter, if you want extra flavour brown your butter. 
add an equal amount of flour to your butter. stir well, toast until golden blonde at least. darker reaux means more flavor, but be careful to not let it burn. 
add your milk a little at a time, whisking vigorously. continue adding milk while whisking until you've got a sauce that is a bit thinner than where you'd like it to end up
add flavoring components - salt, pepper, whatever spices you may want, roasted butternut squash, green chilis, any meat you may want, ETC. 
add your cheeses a handful at a time while stirring. this takes a second, be patient. 
once your cheese is melty and the sauce is smooth, add your heavy cream bit by bit. 
taste for seasoning, make adjustments
add your pasta and reserved pasta water, combine well. remove from heat
transfer to a good casserole dish and top with more cheese. 
bake at 375 for 20-30 minutes or until the cheese on top is either crisped or nicely melted. 
let rest for 5-10 minutes and serve. 
